<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    What groups do to how people feel (Source/ColonyCouncil/Social/Groups/). Belonging is mostly not a mood: a habit
    kept together, a welcome, a joke that lifts someone, a word from the anchor give company, rest or opinion instead
    (RewardInstead), and the heart counts them towards Belonging (their names start with Council_Soc_). What a group
    does against someone (the cold shoulder, being out of step with its ways, a dig from the other lot, a circle
    breaking up) is a small, short bad mood. The left-out feeling stays the social web's Council_Soc_LeftOut, given by
    the groups now, with the group that shut someone out named in its cause.
  -->

  <!-- ===================== Good moments: company, not mood ===================== -->

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Soc_GroupHabit</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilMemory</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>1</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>1</stackLimit>
    <stages><li><label>among my own</label><description>An evening with my own people, doing what we always do. It's good to have a place.</description><baseMoodEffect>0</baseMoodEffect></li></stages>
    <modExtensions><li Class="ColonyCouncil.RewardInstead"><joy>0.05</joy><felt>2</felt><feelings><li>Fellowship</li></feelings></li></modExtensions>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Soc_Welcomed</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilSocial</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>3</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>3</stackLimit>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>1</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages><li><label>made me welcome</label><description>They didn't have to make room for me. They did anyway.</description><baseMoodEffect>0</baseMoodEffect><baseOpinionOffset>6</baseOpinionOffset></li></stages>
    <modExtensions><li Class="ColonyCouncil.RewardInstead"><felt>3</felt></li></modExtensions>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Soc_Lightened</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilSocial</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>2</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>2</stackLimit>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>1</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages><li><label>made me laugh when I needed it</label><description>I was in a black mood, and somehow they got a laugh out of me.</description><baseMoodEffect>0</baseMoodEffect><baseOpinionOffset>4</baseOpinionOffset></li></stages>
    <modExtensions><li Class="ColonyCouncil.RewardInstead"><joy>0.05</joy><felt>2</felt></li></modExtensions>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Soc_Reassured</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilSocial</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>2</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>2</stackLimit>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>1</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages><li><label>talked me down</label><description>I'd worked myself into a state. They listened, and it didn't seem so bad after.</description><baseMoodEffect>0</baseMoodEffect><baseOpinionOffset>3</baseOpinionOffset></li></stages>
    <modExtensions><li Class="ColonyCouncil.RewardInstead"><rest>0.03</rest><felt>2</felt></li></modExtensions>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Soc_CheckedOn</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilSocial</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>2</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>2</stackLimit>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>1</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages><li><label>looked in on me</label><description>They noticed I'd gone quiet, and came to see how I was. That's what they're like.</description><baseMoodEffect>0</baseMoodEffect><baseOpinionOffset>4</baseOpinionOffset></li></stages>
    <modExtensions><li Class="ColonyCouncil.RewardInstead"><felt>2</felt></li></modExtensions>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Soc_InJoke</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilSocial</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>2</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>2</stackLimit>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>1</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages><li><label>our old joke</label><description>Nobody else would understand why it's funny. That's half of why it is.</description><baseMoodEffect>0</baseMoodEffect><baseOpinionOffset>3</baseOpinionOffset></li></stages>
    <modExtensions><li Class="ColonyCouncil.RewardInstead"><joy>0.04</joy><felt>2</felt></li></modExtensions>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!-- ===================== Frictions: small and short ===================== -->

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Grp_ColdShoulder</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilSocial</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>2</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>2</stackLimit>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>1</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages><li><label>the cold shoulder</label><description>I tried to join in. They made it very clear they had all the company they needed.</description><baseMoodEffect>-2</baseMoodEffect><baseOpinionOffset>-8</baseOpinionOffset></li></stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Grp_OutOfStep</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilSocial</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>2</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>2</stackLimit>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>1</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages><li><label>not their sort</label><description>They let me know, not unkindly, that I'm not doing it the way they do it. I'm not sure I want to.</description><baseMoodEffect>-2</baseMoodEffect><baseOpinionOffset>-5</baseOpinionOffset></li></stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Grp_RivalDig</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilSocial</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>1.5</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>2</stackLimit>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>1</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages><li><label>a dig at my lot</label><description>A crack about my people, and I'm supposed to laugh along. Not likely.</description><baseMoodEffect>-1</baseMoodEffect><baseOpinionOffset>-6</baseOpinionOffset></li></stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Grp_CircleBroke</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilMemory</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>4</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>1</stackLimit>
    <stages><li><label>our circle broke apart</label><description>We used to have our evenings, our jokes, our seats. Now it's all sides and silences.</description><baseMoodEffect>-3</baseMoodEffect></li></stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!-- ===================== Opinion from groups (no mood) ===================== -->

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Grp_OneOfUs</defName>
    <thoughtClass>Thought_SituationalSocial</thoughtClass>
    <workerClass>ColonyCouncil.ThoughtWorker_GroupBond</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
    <stages>
      <li><label>one of us</label><baseOpinionOffset>4</baseOpinionOffset></li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Grp_OtherLot</defName>
    <thoughtClass>Thought_SituationalSocial</thoughtClass>
    <workerClass>ColonyCouncil.ThoughtWorker_GroupBond</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
    <stages>
      <li><label>one of that lot</label><baseOpinionOffset>-5</baseOpinionOffset></li>
      <li><label>one of that lot, and they know it</label><baseOpinionOffset>-10</baseOpinionOffset></li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!-- ===================== What groups leave in people's memories (Persona/SharedMemories) ===================== -->

  <ColonyCouncil.SharedMemoryDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Mem_Group_Habit</defName>
    <label>a habit kept together</label>
    <text>{LABEL}, as always</text>
    <weight>0.6</weight>
    <fadeDays>30</fadeDays>
    <valence>1</valence>
  </ColonyCouncil.SharedMemoryDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.SharedMemoryDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Mem_Group_Founded</defName>
    <label>a group begun together</label>
    <text>were among the first of {LABEL}</text>
    <weight>0.8</weight>
    <fadeDays>120</fadeDays>
    <valence>1</valence>
  </ColonyCouncil.SharedMemoryDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.SharedMemoryDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Mem_Group_Split</defName>
    <label>a group come apart</label>
    <text>were on opposite sides when {LABEL} split</text>
    <weight>1</weight>
    <fadeDays>90</fadeDays>
    <valence>-1</valence>
  </ColonyCouncil.SharedMemoryDef>

  <!-- ===================== What helps ===================== -->

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Mood_GroupColdShoulder</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Council_Grp_ColdShoulder</li></thoughts>
    <fix>A group that closes ranks opens up slowly: give the newcomer work alongside its people, let them sit at the same table, and a member who likes them will start speaking for them. A group of warm, trusting people takes newcomers in far sooner.</fix>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Mood_GroupOutOfStep</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Council_Grp_OutOfStep</li></thoughts>
    <fix>They go against their group's ways. In time they either come round a little or drift off to people more like them; work and evenings with others who share their temper help them find their own crowd.</fix>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Mood_GroupRivalDig</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Council_Grp_RivalDig</li></thoughts>
    <fix>Their group and another are at odds (People → Bonds shows why). Feuds between their people and opposed views feed it; ending the feuds, keeping the worst of them on different shifts and good times shared across the groups let it cool.</fix>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Mood_GroupCircleBroke</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Council_Grp_CircleBroke</li></thoughts>
    <fix>It passes in a few days. Those on each side may well find their way into a new group, or back together once the quarrel that split them is over.</fix>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

</Defs>
